 "FINDING_1_VT_AND_SS_ARE_SIMULATED_NOW": "The gate sweep on the ASAP7 nmos_rvt card gives V_t,lin = 0.301 V and V_t,sat = 0.284 V at 300 K (constant-current, 100 nA x W/L), DIBL 26 mV/V, subthreshold swing 61.0 mV/dec. Between 250 and 400 K the threshold falls at -0.39 mV/K (lin) / -0.46 mV/K (sat) and the swing rises at 0.203 mV/dec per K. None of these was available before: V_t was an analytic parameter and SS a single roadmap number.",
 "FINDING_2_THE_TWO_EVIDENCE_FILES_AGREE": "I_off(T) read off the gate sweep at V_gs = 0 reproduces the leakage evidence file's relative curve to 0.76 % at worst across 200.0-500.0 K. Two decks, two sessions, one device.",
 "FINDING_3_THE_VF_SHAPE_IS_SIMULATED_AND_ALPHA_IS_MEASURED": "On the diagonal V_gs = V_ds the alpha-power exponent fitted above threshold is 1.45 at 300 K (rms 0.039 in ln I) against the textbook 1.4 the IRDS model assumes; I_on falls to 0.942 of its 300 K value at 400 K. Normalised to f(vdd), the simulated I_on(V)/V shape and the IRDS alpha-power shape differ by at most 43.6 % over 0.45-0.77 V. With the trace's 3.8 GHz at 0.70 V as the anchor, the device curve puts the 10 % overdrive ceiling at 4.17 GHz.",
 "FINDING_4_THE_VT_LEVER_ON_THE_DEVICE": "A 50 mV V_t reduction at 300 K buys 15.1 % clock on the simulated curve (13.1 % on IRDS) and costs 6.59x leakage at the simulated 61.0 mV/dec (4.07x at the roadmap's 82); at 400 K the same 50 mV costs 4.13x because the swing has risen to 81.2 mV/dec, and the simulated leakage curve's local doubling temperature there is 23.3 K, so 47.7 K of cooling pays for it.",
 "HONEST_LIMITS": "One device (nmos_rvt), one drawn length, no self-heating, no p-FET, no wire load, and a threshold CRITERION (100 nA x W/L) that is a convention -- compare temperature coefficients and shapes across sources, never levels. The absolute V/F anchor is the trace's clock at the card's nominal supply and is a statement about where the trace sits on the curve, not a measured ASAP7 clock."
}